ats on the side of  four houses i've got a seat i think  very very hot a number of males around  it this time  police body worn camera recorded the  moment officers arrested henry long  and albert bowers on far more serious  charges  than the theft of a quad bike i'm  arresting both of you  on suspicion of murder  all right and that's of a thames valley  police officer so it's suspicious  of a thames family police officer does  it look like i've done a murder  guy  calling me a murderer all right so do  you two both understand  the suspects had been caught on cctv in  the hours before the robbery  driving around the local area looking  for items to steal  before settling on the quad bike later  that night  as the bike's owner spotted them he  dialed nine nine nine  ten sally please watch emergency i've  got four masked men outside my house and  they've got weapons  oh and they're stealing my squad bike  i'm going out there now no no don't go  out there i'm going out there no because  throughout this has been a highly  complex case  the jury taken on a site visit to the  spot where pc harper  was dragged to his death a computer  reconstruction  helping explain the precise sequence of  events  it has been a very difficult case  because when uh the crown prosecution  service and thames valley police  joined forces we had 10 in custody and  obviously they'd all been arrested from  the caravan site with no one saying  anything there was no  forensic evidence or in fact direct  evidence to link  anyone with the vehicle and so it was  analysis of  phones particularly that linked henry  long  and albert bowers to the offense  by all accounts andrew harper was an  extremely popular  and dedicated officer he'd been married  just  four weeks before the tragic events that  ended his life  he and his colleague were at the end of  their shift but still decided to respond  to the robbery  his senseless death an illustration of  the highly unpredictable nature of the  job  no offic